# 1️⃣ Single Stage Build

A Single Stage Dockerfile performs everything in one image.

Example:

```dockerfile
FROM node:20

WORKDIR /app

COPY . .

CMD ["node","app.js"]
```

### Advantages

- Easy to understand
- Good for beginners

### Disadvantages

- Large image size
- Build dependencies remain inside image
- Less secure
- Not recommended for production

---

# 2️⃣ Multi-Stage Build

Multi-stage build separates the build environment from the runtime environment.

Example:

```dockerfile
# Stage 1 - Builder
FROM node:20 AS builder

WORKDIR /app

COPY . .

RUN echo "building app..."


# Stage 2 - Runtime
FROM node:20-alpine

WORKDIR /app

COPY --from=builder /app /app

CMD ["node","app.js"]
```

---

# 3️⃣ Understanding Stages

## Stage 1 (Builder)

Purpose:

- Build application
- Install dependencies
- Compile project
- Generate build files

Everything happens here.

---

## Stage 2 (Runtime)

Purpose:

- Copy only required files
- Ignore unnecessary build tools
- Produce smaller image

